That wouldn't have worked anyway, since minotaurs (as do A and @) do not
respect Elbereth.

And the problem was not that you were level 13, it was that you used the
wrong tactics for fighting one with not very good HP and AC. 150 HP, AC
-10 and no half-physical-damage is not enough for meleeing a minotaur.

It can get a double move on any character (even a very fast character)
but if you already have some distance you can outrun it if you're fast
or very fast.

As they have 0% MR% and a poor AC (6) many magical effects such as
sleep, taming, polymorph, death work well. Teleportation works well, as
on about any non-covetous monster.

Digging down can also be good, except on the castle level. On the way
up, you can magic map the level or quaff a cursed potion of gain level.

Good ranged weapons sometimes work (note they must be really good,
expertly thrown +0 daggers with 18 strength are probably insufficient).

I often genocide them from thrones. Other 'H' are rarely worth
genociding.

The moral is that any early-castle-assault plan must include something
for minotaurs.

